  "details": "**This is not visible to yourself, it is only an issue to others looking at you.**\n\nThis is happening with both fresh uploads AND older ones. \n\nEven if my avatar is medium rated OR the other user is friend and have my avatars shown entirely across the board, the finger tracking data just won't be sent unless they hide and re-show the particular avatar. \n\nAt first I thought it was something to do with my newest avatar - it has physbones on the fingers as they're wing-hands. This bug was appearing on others wearing this same avatar.\n\nBut then I see it happening on some of my older personal avatars as well that do NOT have physbones on the fingers, and have to remind friends to show/hide my avatars, even if they're Medium rated.\n\nOnly correlation between the avatars seems to be that they have non-stock humanoid hands? The one is a owl with wing-hands, the other is a dragon with only two fingers and a thumb meshed, but both have technically the proper full set of four fingers and a thumb *rigged* and recognized in Unity. \n\nIt seems to be a visual thing with the data being shown/sent to others. I don't know how to fix it or even where to start to fix it. I need it to be fixed for the owl specially as that's an avatar I intend to sell.",
